# Line endings are part of repository truth here, not a formatting preference.
#
# The change engine hashes bytes and diffs lines. The evaluation corpus declares
# gold symbol ranges, evidence line numbers, and content hashes against files as
# they were authored — with LF. Without this file Git's `core.autocrlf` rewrites
# them to CRLF on any Windows checkout, every fixture hash changes, and the
# Phase 4 corpus fails on a fresh clone while passing for whoever wrote it.
#
# So: normalized in the repository, LF in the working tree, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The one deliberate exception to the rule above, and the reason it is narrow.
#
# ADR-0043 records that a checkout whose line endings Git rewrote made preflight
# call every line of every file changed while `git status` was empty. The corpus
# could never see that defect precisely *because* of the `eol=lf` rule above:
# both sides are LF, so there is nothing to disagree about. The c028 target is
# therefore the only file in this repository allowed to keep CRLF bytes through
# a checkout. Marking it `-text` — not `binary` — keeps it diffable.
#
# Do not "fix" the line endings of this file. Its bytes are the test.
tests/evaluation/cases/variants/python_app/crlf-only/target/src/payments/service.py -text

# Binary formats must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.sqlite binary
*.db binary
